 # Changelog
 
+## 0.4.5 (2026-10-18)
+
+Additive only (no existing item changed; `Options`, `LeaseOptions` and `LeaseInfo` are `#[non_exhaustive]`, so the new fields are not breaking). Not compiled or run when written.
+
+- Additive (feature `fs`, `lease`; Orthic-Labs/rightkit#478): the lease record names its holder. `LeaseInfo::{exe, kind}` and `LeaseOptions::kind(..)` (`LeaseOptions::kind` field); `exe` is `std::env::current_exe` taken at acquire, `kind` is the caller's role word; `LeaseInfo::is_this_process()`. The record keeps header `rightkit-lease v1` and gains `exe=` and `kind=` lines; a 0.4.4 record without them still parses (both empty) and a 0.4.4 reader ignores them. Holder takeover (dead pid), heartbeat-TTL expiry of a hung live holder and `peek` were already in 0.4.4; tests added for the 0.4.4 record shape and for the new fields.
+- Additive (feature `fs`; #738): `publish_group(&[GroupEntry], &GroupOptions) -> GroupPublished { published, replaced, unsynced, leftover_backups }`, a multi-file publish with backup (hard link, else copy, `.<name>.rkbak-<pid>-<n>`), rollback of every published file on failure, and a cancel gate (`GroupOptions::cancel`, asked before the backups and before each file; a cancel is `FsError::Io` of kind `Interrupted`). Validates first (regular staging files, no symlink or directory destination, no duplicate destination). Not one atomic step for a concurrent reader.
+- Additive (feature `fs`; #738): `remove_tree(root, &RemoveOptions) -> Result<bool>`, a directory-tree removal that retries Windows sharing, lock, access-denied and delete-pending errors (`RemoveOptions { attempts: 8, delay: 50 ms }`), clears the read-only attribute, removes a link inside the tree as an entry without following it, refuses a link or file root, and returns `Ok(false)` for a missing root.
+- Additive (feature `app-dirs`; #738): `Options::data_dir_override(Option<PathBuf>)` (field `Options::data_dir`), a release data-folder override with no environment variable and no feature gate (same layout as the QA override, `isolated` true, absolute and `..` checked); `AppDirs::is_real_user_path(&app, path)` and `AppDirs::is_real_user_path_with(app, os, env, path)`, true for a path at or inside the app's real per-user folders (both namespaces, every legacy name, with and without org) or equal to the home folder or above it. The QA override check now shares the same folder list (and also covers legacy names).
+- Additive (feature `fs`; #732, #613): `StableId` and `new_stable_id()` are defined in `file_key` and exported at the crate root with feature `fs` alone (`rightkit_fs::StableId`, `rightkit_fs::new_stable_id`); `identity::StableId` still resolves to the same type and the ledger still needs `json`.
+- Additive (feature `fs`; #712): `migrate_dir_marked(from, to, &MarkOptions) -> MarkedMigration { migrated, marker }` and `is_marked(dir, &MarkOptions)`: `migrate_dir` that also leaves `migrated-from.json` (`from`, `at_ms`, optional `note`) in the new folder. The marker is written into the source tree first, so `to` never appears without it, and a refused move puts the source's marker state back. `migrate_dir` already moved by rename and set aside an empty destination; unchanged.
+- Additive (#388): `test_mode` module (no feature for the pure parts): `decide`, `Variables`, `Guard`, `TestMode`, `build::{Spec, ReleaseGuard, Resolved, resolve, emit}` (the `build.rs` helper that turns the app's features into the `test_mode_enabled` cfg with a release guard), `forbid_in_release!`; with feature `test-mode`, `init_or_exit`, `current`, `select`, and the embedded `COMPILED_MARKER`. A relative path, `..`, the home folder, user folders, the app's real folders and a symlink into them are refused.
+- Additive (feature `app-dirs`; #765): `app_dirs::user_dirs::{home, desktop, documents, downloads}`, each `fn() -> Option<PathBuf>`, the values of `dirs` 6/7: Windows asks `SHGetKnownFolderPath` (no environment fallback), macOS is `$HOME` plus `Desktop`, `Documents`, `Downloads`, Linux and other unix read `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/user-dirs.dirs` (else `~/.config/user-dirs.dirs`). They ignore the test root and QA overrides. XDG parsing is unit tested.
+- Docs (#710 item 4): `zip::read_zip` documents that entry names are untrusted.
+
 ## 0.4.4 (2026-10-18)
 
 - Additive (feature `fs`): `lease` module (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#478): `Lease::try_acquire(path, &LeaseOptions) -> Acquire { Acquired(Lease), Held(LeaseInfo) }`, `Lease::renew`, `Lease::release` (also on drop), `Lease::peek`, `LeaseInfo::staleness() -> Staleness { Fresh, HolderDead, Expired }`. A pid + heartbeat-TTL lease record in a plain file, created exclusively (`ReplaceMode::NoReplace`) and heartbeated by atomic replace. Stale means the holder pid is confirmed dead (the crate's tri-state probe: `kill(pid, 0)` on Unix, `OpenProcess`/`GetExitCodeProcess` plus a complete process snapshot on Windows; an unknown probe is never dead) or the last heartbeat is older than the holder's TTL (or more than a TTL in the future). A stale record is renamed aside, checked, and replaced; a renewing holder whose record was taken learns it from `FsError::Locked`. Not `FileLock`: it is a record, not an OS lock, and it never sleeps or polls. Local machine only. Not compiled or run when written.
