 - `test-seams` (allowed in release builds): `atomic::seams`, for a consumer's tests that run in the release profile. `fail_write_after(bytes, kind)` makes this thread's `AtomicWriter::write_all` / `AtomicWriter::writer()` writes fail after `bytes` bytes (the bytes up to the limit are written first); `sync_counts()`, `take_sync_counts()` and `reset_sync_counts()` count the file flushes and directory syncs this thread attempted. Per thread, inert until installed. It does not see a write made through `AtomicWriter::file_mut()` or the `File` an `atomic_write_with*` closure receives.
 
+## Test-mode gate (`test_mode`)
+
+`test_mode::decide` / `init_or_exit` / `current` give a desktop app one start-of-process decision (`Off`, `On { data_dir }`, `Refuse`) from an app-named service variable and isolated-data-directory variable, refusing a relative path, `..`, the home folder, user folders, the app's real folders and symlinks into them. `test_mode::build::emit` is the `build.rs` helper that turns the app's features into the `test_mode_enabled` cfg with a release guard, and `forbid_in_release!` is the `compile_error!` form. The run-time reader needs feature `test-mode`; the pure parts and the build helper need none.
+
+## Leases, group publish, tree removal, marked migration
+
+- `lease::Lease` (feature `fs`): a pid + heartbeat-TTL lease file. `Lease::try_acquire(path, &LeaseOptions::new(ttl).label(..).kind("daemon"))` gives `Acquired(lease)` or `Held(info)`; `renew` heartbeats (call at least every `ttl / 3`), `release` or drop gives it up, `Lease::peek` reads the holder without taking it. A holder whose pid is confirmed dead, or whose heartbeat is older than its TTL (a hung live process), is taken over. `LeaseInfo` carries `pid`, `exe` (the holder's executable path), `kind`, `label`, `ttl`, `acquired_ms` and `heartbeat_ms`.
+- `publish_group(&[GroupEntry::new(staged, dest)], &GroupOptions::new().cancel(&gate))`: several finished files published as a group. Existing destinations are backed up first (hard link, else copy), the files are published one by one with a cancel check before each, and a failure or cancel rolls every published file back. Not one atomic step for a concurrent reader; all-or-nothing for the outcome.
+- `remove_tree(root, &RemoveOptions::default())`: `remove_dir_all` that retries Windows sharing and lock violations, clears read-only files, never follows a link inside the tree and refuses a link as the root. `Ok(false)` when the root is already gone.
+- `migrate_dir_marked(from, to, &MarkOptions::new().note(..))` and `is_marked(dir, &MarkOptions::new())`: `migrate_dir` that leaves `migrated-from.json` in the new folder (written into the source first, so it moves with the tree).
+- `StableId` and `new_stable_id()` need only feature `fs`; the ledger (`IdentityStore`) needs `json`.
+- `Options::data_dir_override(Some(dir))` roots an `AppDirs` under a directory the app supplies, in a release build, with no variable and no feature; `AppDirs::is_real_user_path(&app, path)` says whether a path is one of the app's real per-user folders (or the home folder, or above it).
+- `app_dirs::user_dirs::{home, desktop, documents, downloads}`: the account's own folders, the values the `dirs` crate gives.
+
 ## State directories (`StateDir`)
 
 `StateDir::open`/`create` use `StateOptions::default()`; `open_with`/`create_with` take explicit options. Children from `child` inherit them.
